{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChDFpTJ6bxsAaN7VijDva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I marked `tc_irq_handler` in `samples/s223.c` as **not vulnerable** and wrote that to `results/s223.json`. It looks like an already-fixed version of the interrupt handler:\n\n- **Failed or empty status read:** if reading `INTSTS_G` fails or returns 0, the handler exits early.\n- **Uninitialized value:** `stat` is set to 0 before `regmap_read(SYSSTAT, ...)`. If that read fails, the error message logs 0 instead of uninitialized stack memory.\n- **NULL pointer:** before calling `drm_kms_helper_hotplug_event()`, the handler checks that `hpd_pin >= 0` and that `tc->bridge.dev` and `tc->aux.drm_dev` are set. So an interrupt that arrives before the bridge is attached can't trigger a NULL dereference.\n\nThe one small gap is that the handler ignores whether the `SYSSTAT` read succeeded. That can only make the log message misleading, not unsafe, so I put it in `suggested_fix` as optional hardening rather than listing it as a vulnerability."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":22447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":702},"output_tokens":373,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f105e5b-12d0-432d-a407-67e263779c57","uuid":"e29d15de-7e58-40cf-b8a9-0d01b7e4fff2","timestamp":"2026-11-20T00:45:51.558Z","request_id":"req_011ChDFpT9B9XWAmESx6nFqu"}
